// "+2/+0 for each <selection>" scaled pump ([CR#613.4c] layer 7c, [CR#107.3]
// "for each") — the coefficient-2 twin of `P1P0ForEach` (Goblin Piledriver's
// shape). Predicate slot = the selection noun; Objects+CountOf wrap it, then
// `Times(Literal(2), ...)` doubles the count before it feeds the sole power
// axis. NO toughness node — the printed "/+0" is template-literal text, not a
// real scaling axis. Render flattens this through the structural
// `for_each_pump_clause` arm (which recognizes the `Times(Literal(n),
// CountOf(Objects(pred)))` coefficient shape) — the template is parse-only.
(
    name: "P2P0ForEach",
    template: "gets +2/+0 for each ${0}",
    kinds: [Modification],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Power(Up(Times(Literal(2), CountOf(Objects(Param(0)))))),
)
